! mcp_bootstrap_p138.strap -- MCP printed page 138, the tail of the
! console EDIT routine plus the whole of P CSRD (the fake-read
! routine) and the head of G TRANF (the TRANSFER SUBROUTINE).
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.145.
!
! HEADER READ, NOT ASSUMED.  The top line prints
!   "TIME CLOCK 00054041   PUNID 11011MCP   CARD ID EE000167
!    DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 138"
! and the column-header line below it prints
!   "LINE   LOCATION   BINARY OUTPUT   NAME   STATEMENT   LOCATION
!    217056".
!
! >>> THE COLUMN-HEADER LINE CARRIES A SECOND "LOCATION" FIELD, AND
! IT IS A FREE ORIGIN WITNESS. <<<  Far to the right of "STATEMENT"
! this page prints "LOCATION  217056" -- the WORD at which the page
! begins, printed by IBM's own assembler in the page header.  Read
! at 600 dpi from x=5800 y=380 (600-dpi units).  It is not a
! substitute for line 1's own 217056.40 (the header gives no bit
! offset), but it is an independent confirmation of the word, and it
! is the cheapest join check in this volume.  No deck in this
! repository has used it; it should be read on every page from here
! on.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! 56 printed lines.  48 carry a LOCATION; 8 are comment cards
! (lines 10, 17, 18, 19, 20, 43, 52, 56 -- LOCATION and BINARY
! OUTPUT both empty, text printed raw from card column 2).
! First printed location 217056.40 (line 1), last 217115.00
! (line 55).  Card serials EE000167..EE000221, and EE000194 IS
! PUNCHED TWICE, on lines 28 and 29 -- read at 1200 dpi, not
! inferred: the column prints 192, 193, 194, 194, 195, 196.  That
! is 55 distinct serials over 56 cards.  Nothing rests on it; the
! row count is pinned by the LINE column (1..56) and by the closed
! address chain below.
!
! Three locations carry an asterisk after them: lines 11, 33 and
! 55 (217065.40 *, 217101.00 *, 217115.00 *).  Recorded, not
! explained -- printed p.136 carries the same mark on four of its
! rows and no deck has yet established what it flags.
!
! THE ADDRESS CHAIN CLOSES END TO END.  Every row's printed address
! plus its own length (one half word, or one full word for lines 1,
! 2, 3, 4, 9, 11, 22, 23, 25, 26, 33, 38, 44, 54, 55) equals the
! next row's printed address, across all forty-eight of them, with
! no gap and no overlap.  Line 55 is a full word, so the counter
! reaches 217116.00 for printed p.139.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOINS, BOTH WITNESSED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> BACKWARD, to printed p.137. <<<  This page prints no SLC, so
! the "SLC,(8)217056.40" below is an ASSERTION and a hard SLC
! cannot disagree with the counter arriving from the previous page
! (docs/transcription_workflow.md, "WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE",
! item 2).  Two things support it, neither of them this page's own
! ink:
!   (a) the page header's own "LOCATION 217056" (above), which is
!       printed on THIS page and so is not an independent witness
!       for the join, but is independent of my reading of line 1;
!   (b) the volume OCR of printed p.137 -- a DIFFERENT page, so a
!       legitimate (if garbled) second reader -- whose last row is
!       "217056.00  000011.11 50  SC,$4,$R  -YES-PUT EDITED CHAR.
!       COUNT IN $R", a HALF word at 217056.00, which leaves the
!       counter at exactly 217056.40.
! printed p.137 is being transcribed in parallel and its deck must
! land on 217056.40; if it does not, this SLC is the thing to
! re-examine.
!
! >>> FORWARD, to printed p.139. <<<  Line 54 branches to G SKIPA,
! and the branch's second half word prints "217116.34 02" -- bit 18
! of 0o34 is clear, so the target is the .00 half word of 217116.
! That is exactly where this page's counter stops.  The volume OCR
! carries p.139's defining card, "217116.00  000036.05 50  G SKIPA
! SC,$2,$14".  So the last row of this page and the first row of
! the next are joined by a branch printed here.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> ONE ROW IS LEFT FAILING.  LINE 11's "M-" IS AN ASSEMBLER GAP
! AND THE STATEMENT BELOW IS A PLACEHOLDER, NOT A TRANSCRIPTION. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The page prints, at 217065.40:
!
!    11*  217065.40 *  000025.00 80  030000.30 90   M-(BU,24),$5
!                                                   -FROM THE MSG
!
! strap_asm raises a bare KeyError 'M-' on "M-(BU,24),$5": the VFL
! dispatch has no entry for the written-minus form, although the
! FLOATING-POINT path in the same file knows the rule exactly --
! see strap/strap_asm.py ~line 1405, "M- is M+ with the negative
! sign modifier (printed code 22355.50 A0 vs M+'s .40)".
!
! THE ARITHMETIC MAKES THIS A PRECISE GAP RATHER THAN A MYSTERY:
!
!    M+(BU,24),$5   assembles   000025.00 80  030000.20 90
!    the page prints            000025.00 80  030000.30 90
!    difference                                      0o10
!
! and 0o10 in that field is exactly the difference the assembler's
! own FP note records between M- and M+ (.50 against .40).  So the
! reading is confirmed three ways: the glyph at 1800 dpi is an
! unambiguous "M-"; the comment ("REMOVE PREVIOUS NON BACKSPACE
! CHAR- FROM THE MSG", lines 9-11) is a SUBTRACTION; and the
! printed bits are M+ plus the one documented sign bit.
!
! RESOLVED: strap_asm now admits "M-" on a VFL operation (this page and
! printed p.142 line 4 are the two witnesses that admitted it).  The row
! below is the PRINTED form and it passes.
! COUNTER RIGHT -- M+ and M- are the same length, so every row
! after line 11 still lands on its printed address.  The !CHECK for
! this row carries the PRINTED bits "030000.30 90", so IT FAILS,
! deliberately and loudly.
!
! >>> DO NOT "FIX" THAT CHECK TO .20. <<<  Changing it would make
! the page pass while compiling an ADD where IBM compiled a
! SUBTRACT.  The fix belongs in strap_asm's VFL dispatch: give it
! the same written-minus rule the FP path already has.  When it
! lands, change the statement line back to the printed "M-" and the
! check passes untouched.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! A SECOND, NARROWER GAP: A BLANK INSIDE A NAME INSIDE AN
! EXPRESSION
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 25 prints "CM0000(BU,1), S CNS SG+1.0($1),0".  strap_asm
! accepts blanks in a name in a bare address field (the house
! examples are "B, P ERR EX" and "VF,S ASPUT") but NOT when the
! name is followed by an arithmetic operator: the printed form
! raises "line N: undefined symbol 'S'" -- the expression parser
! splits on "+" first and then on the blank.  The deck writes
! "SCNSSG+1.0($1),0", which assembles BIT-IDENTICALLY to the
! printed row, and the printed form is kept in the !CHECK note.
! Line 38's "SCNSSG($1)" is printed closed up already and needs no
! substitution, which is what isolates the failure to the
! expression path.
!
! Everything else on the page was handed to strap_asm AS PRINTED
! and accepted, including the forms that have cost pages before:
!   "(2)1111 1110"        a BLANK INSIDE A RADIX LITERAL (line 3).
!                         TESTED, not assumed: it assembles to the
!                         printed 774000.00 80 410000.20 50.  This
!                         was silently miscompiling until 36290f2.
!   ",0($2)" ",3.0($3)"   a BLANK OPERATION FIELD (lines 30-32),
!   ",$R"                 the three parameter half words of the
!                         B,GTRANF calling sequence.
!   "LVE,$3,($15)"        an OMITTED ADDRESS before an index.
!   "*I(BU,18),8,46"      multiply immediate (line 1).
!   "LX,$4,$2"            a register as a bare address.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE C/0 QUESTION, AND WHY LINE 5's BYTE IS 00
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! This drum opens round glyphs constantly.  Line 5 reads, at 900
! dpi, "CCCC01.11 CO" -- and the first four characters sit in an
! OCTAL field, which cannot hold a C, so they are certainly 0 and
! this row demonstrably drops ink on round glyphs before it reaches
! the byte.  That is NOT a licence to convert the byte (ink varies
! per CHARACTER).  WHAT SETTLES IT IS WHAT PRODUCED IT:
!   (a) line 14 on this page is the SAME instruction with the other
!       sign, "C-I,$4,1.0", and prints "000001.11 08".  C+I and C-I
!       differ by the sign bit alone, so C+I's byte is 00 and C-I's
!       is 08 -- there is no reading in which C+I prints C0 and C-I
!       prints 08;
!   (b) printed p.136 line 5 is a landed "C+I,$4,8.0" whose !CHECK
!       passes at "000010.11 00".
! The deck writes 00.  The same reasoning covers line 25's and line
! 38's "001000.CC FO" (= 001000.00 F0, CM0000 with no second-operand
! index, matching p.136 line 35's landed row) and line 44's
! "217134.CC AC" (= 217134.00 A0, a Transmit whose second operand
! carries no index, so the low nibble i2 is 0).
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! TWO GLYPHS SETTLED AT 1800 dpi
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! "G DIAR" (lines 8 and 12).  The third character has a STRAIGHT
! VERTICAL LEFT STEM and squared corners, against the round
! stemless C of "KCI" in the row below it and the round 0 of
! "LI(BU,24),8" in the row above.  It is a D.
!
! "G VODR" (line 44).  The STATEMENT prints a CLOSED O in position
! 2 and a stemmed D in position 3; the COMMENT in the same row
! prints the same word with position 2 OPEN.  Dropout opens a
! closed glyph and never closes an open one, so the closed reading
! wins: V-O-D-R.  The volume OCR's four readings of this symbol on
! OTHER pages are VOCR, VCDR, VODR and VCCR -- all four consistent
! with V-O-D-R and with nothing else -- and p.139's defining card
! reads "217134.00 *  000020.00  G VODR  DRZ(BU,64),16  -RESERVE 16
! FULL WORDS", sixteen words, which is exactly the count line 44
! transmits ("TI,16.0,$0,G VODR  -SAVE $0-$15 IN LOC. G VODR").
!
! "G OKOLO" (line 15) AND "G KOLO" (line 51) ARE TWO DIFFERENT
! SYMBOLS, not one misread.  Line 15's CB prints 217047.12 and line
! 51 is DEFINED here at 217113.00.  The volume OCR carries p.137's
! defining card at 217047.00 ("G CKOLC  L(V+I)(BU,8),.8($4)  -LOAD
! A CHAR.") and p.137's own reference "217054.40  217047.12 48
! CB,$5,G CKOLG" -- the same instruction to the same word, one page
! earlier.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! TAIL SCOPE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." moved the origin, and
! pp.99+ are OUTSIDE the TAIL,(2)G block that printed p.2 opened
! and printed p.98 line 37 closed.  Names here may legitimately
! repeat names defined in pp.2-98 at different addresses.  None of
! this page's twelve labels collides with a pp.2-98 name in any
! landed deck.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS.  WHAT IS READ AND WHAT IS CONVENTION
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> AN ADDRESS BACK-DERIVED FROM A BRANCH OR AN LVI IS PINNED
! ONLY TO THE HALF WORD. <<<  Bit offsets 0-31 all encode
! identically; only bit 18, the half-word select, shows.  Writing
! ".0" is a CONVENTION and no !CHECK here can test below it.  The
! half word ITSELF is checked and does catch errors, which is why
! the ".40" values are written as read.
!
! A VFL CONNECTIVE'S OPERAND ADDRESS IS A BIT ADDRESS AND IS FULLY
! PRINTED, so the symbols derived from lines 4, 22, 23, 33 and 44
! are read to the bit.
!
! GMISTO  217012.00  FULLY OBSERVED HERE, and more strongly than on
!                    printed p.136, which back-derived it from an
!                    LVI.  Line 4 is a VFL connective whose operand
!                    address is a BIT address: it prints
!                    "217012.00 86".  Line 7's "KVI,$5, G MISTO"
!                    prints 217012.13, the same word a second way.
!                    LANDED at this value by decks/
!                    mcp_bootstrap_p136.strap.
GMISTO  SYN, (8)217012.0
! GOKOLO  217047.00  NEW.  Line 15's CB prints "217047.12 48";
!                    0o12 = $5*2, bit 18 clear, so the target is
!                    the .00 half word.  DEFINED on printed p.137
!                    (volume OCR, defining card at 217047.00).
GOKOLO  SYN, (8)217047.0
! GKONTR  217055.00  NEW.  Line 16 prints "217055.10 00"; 0o10 is
!                    the unconditional-branch code, bit 18 clear.
!                    DEFINED on printed p.137 (volume OCR:
!                    "217055.00  000120.11 0A  G KONTR  KCI,$4,80
!                    -HAVE EDITED 80 CHARS WITHOUT ENCOUNTERING AN
!                    END CODE").
GKONTR  SYN, (8)217055.0
! GVODR   217134.00  NEW, AND FULLY OBSERVED.  Line 44's Transmit
!                    prints its second operand's address as
!                    "217134.00 A0" -- a storage address with its
!                    bit offset.  Defined on printed p.139.
GVODR   SYN, (8)217134.0
! GHI     217132.40  NEW.  Lines 50 and 53 print "217132.70 42" and
!                    "217132.73 42"; bit 18 of both is SET, so the
!                    .40 half word IS observed and IS checked.  Two
!                    independent rows, two different conditions,
!                    the same half word.  Defined on printed p.139
!                    (volume OCR: "217132.40  000021.04 50  G HI
!                    LC,$2,$1").
GHI     SYN, (8)217132.40
! GSKIPA  217116.00  NEW.  Line 54's second half word prints
!                    "217116.34 02", bit 18 clear.  Defined on
!                    printed p.139, the page this one runs into.
GSKIPA  SYN, (8)217116.0
! KNORM   215776.00  LANDED by decks/mcp_bootstrap_p128.strap.
!                    Line 35 prints "215776.03 01", the same
!                    reference printed p.136 line 45 carries.
KNORM   SYN, (8)215776.0
! KGATE   215746.40  LANDED by decks/mcp_bootstrap_p123.strap
!                    (label row).  Line 36 prints "215746.50 00" --
!                    0o50 is 0o40 plus the branch code 0o10, so the
!                    half word IS observed.
KGATE   SYN, (8)215746.40
! PPPBF   216760.00  LANDED by decks/mcp_bootstrap_p136.strap, whose
!                    line 52 prints "216760.32 A0".  Line 24 here
!                    prints "216760.05 01" ($2*2+1 = 0o05), the
!                    same word from an LVI.
PPPBF   SYN, (8)216760.0
! PMCPBF  216775.00  LANDED by decks/mcp_bootstrap_p136.strap.
!                    Line 37 prints "216775.05 01".
PMCPBF  SYN, (8)216775.0
! SUNA    0.0        LANDED as a communication-region field offset
!                    by decks/mcp_bootstrap_p103.strap et al
!                    ("SUNA SYN(BU,25), 0.0", printed p.99 line 20
!                    "S UN A  SYN, S UN A A").  Line 21's
!                    "LV,$1,SUNA($10)" prints "000000.02 3A": the
!                    0o02 is $1*2, the index field, so this row
!                    pins only the WORD (0), not the bit offset.
SUNA    SYN(BU,25), 0.0
! SCW     3.0        LANDED by decks/mcp_bootstrap_p102.strap
!                    ("S CW  SYN(BU,64),3.0  -CONTROL WORD").  Line
!                    22's VFL operand prints "000003.00 8D", which
!                    reads the bit offset too.
SCW     SYN(BU,64), 3.0
! SCCW    4.0        LANDED by decks/mcp_bootstrap_p102.strap
!                    ("S CCW SYN(BU,64),4.0 -COPIED CONTROL WORD").
!                    Line 33 prints "000004.00 8D".
SCCW    SYN(BU,64), 4.0
! SL      215001.04  LANDED by decks/mcp_bootstrap_p103.strap
!                    (printed p.103 line 14, SCOMRG+0.04, -LEVEL OF
!                    INSTRUCTION).  Line 23 prints "215001.04 80",
!                    a one-bit VFL operand read to the bit.
SL      SYN(BU,1), (8)215001.04
! SCNSSG  0.47       LANDED by decks/mcp_bootstrap_p103.strap
!                    (-CONSOLE SIGNAL).  0.47 is a BARE DECIMAL
!                    literal -- bit 47 decimal -- and prints as
!                    0o57, which is what lines 25 and 38 show
!                    ("000001.57" = SCNSSG+1.0, "000000.57" =
!                    SCNSSG).
SCNSSG  SYN(BU,1), 0.47
!
! >>> THIS PAGE RETIRES TWO OF printed p.136's CAVEATS. <<<
! p.136 back-derived GKONEC from a SIC and POUT from a VFL
! connective and wrote, correctly, that the bit offsets were
! convention.  This page carries BOTH DEFINING CARDS: line 6 is
! "G KONEC  B,$" at 217063.00 and line 42 is "P OUT  VF, 0.0" at
! 217106.40.  Both land on exactly p.136's values, and POUT's .40
! is now read off a printed LOCATION rather than inferred.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
        SLC,(8)217056.40

        *I(BU,18),8,46                  ! line  1   217056.40
        ST(BU,25), $6,19                ! line  2   217057.40
        LI(BU,8),(2)1111 1110           ! line  3   217060.40
        CM0101(BU,8),GMISTO($6)         ! line  4   217061.40
        C+I,$4,1                        ! line  5   217062.40
GKONEC  B,$                             ! line  6   217063.00
GVRAT   KVI,$5,GMISTO                   ! line  7   217063.40
        BXE,GDIAR                       ! line  8   217064.00
        LI(BU,24),8                     ! line  9   217064.40
!       >>> LINE 11 IS "M-(BU,24),$5" AND THE LINE BELOW IS A
!       PLACEHOLDER THAT KEEPS THE COUNTER.  ITS !CHECK FAILS BY
!       THE ONE SIGN BIT, ON PURPOSE.  SEE THE HEAD OF THIS FILE.
        M-(BU,24),$5                    ! line 11   217065.40
GDIAR   KCI,$4,0                        ! line 12   217066.40
        BXE,$+1.0                       ! line 13   217067.00
        C-I,$4,1.0                      ! line 14   217067.40
        CB,$5,GOKOLO                    ! line 15   217070.00
        B,GKONTR                        ! line 16   217070.40
PCSRD   LV,$1,SUNA($10)                 ! line 21   217071.00
        C0011(BU),SCW($13),0            ! line 22   217071.40
        BB,SL,PMCP                      ! line 23   217072.40
        LVI,$2,PPPBF                    ! line 24   217073.40
        CM0000(BU,1),SCNSSG+1.0($1),0   ! line 25   217074.00
PCSRD1  BZB,2.63($2),P3WD               ! line 26   217075.00
        LV,$3,POUT                      ! line 27   217076.00
PCSRD2  LVI,$15,$+1.0                   ! line 28   217076.40
        B,GTRANF                        ! line 29   217077.00
        ,0($2)                          ! line 30   217077.40
        ,3.0($3)                        ! line 31   217100.00
        ,$R                             ! line 32   217100.40
        ST(BU),SCCW($13),64             ! line 33   217101.00
        LCI,$7,(8)40.0                  ! line 34   217102.00
        LVI,$1,KNORM                    ! line 35   217102.40
        B,KGATE                         ! line 36   217103.00
PMCP    LVI,$2,PMCPBF                   ! line 37   217103.40
        CM0000(BU,1),SCNSSG($1)         ! line 38   217104.00
        B,PCSRD1                        ! line 39   217105.00
P3WD    LVI,$3,0                        ! line 40   217105.40
        B,PCSRD2                        ! line 41   217106.00
POUT    VF,0.0                          ! line 42   217106.40
GTRANF  TI,16.0,$0,GVODR                ! line 44   217107.00
        LVE,$1,.32($15)                 ! line 45   217110.00
        LVE,$3,($15)                    ! line 46   217110.40
        LVE,$2,1.0($15)                 ! line 47   217111.00
        LX,$2,0.0($2)                   ! line 48   217111.40
        LX,$4,$2                        ! line 49   217112.00
        BXCZ,GHI                        ! line 50   217112.40
GKOLO   KC,$2,$1                        ! line 51   217113.00
        BXH,GHI                         ! line 53   217113.40
GSKIP   BB,$2+.27,GSKIPA                ! line 54   217114.00
        T,$2,0.0($3),0.0($2)            ! line 55   217115.00

